    "field": "Paleoclimate modeling",
    "problem": "Although suppressed ENSO activity during the mid-Holocene is well-documented, a consensus on the underlying physical mechanisms is lacking, as previous modeling studies have provided diverse and potentially model-dependent interpretations.",
    "method": "This study employs the Bjerknes stability index to quantitatively diagnose dynamic and thermodynamic air-sea feedbacks from PMIP simulations, thereby identifying the key physical processes responsible for the suppressed ENSO activity during the mid-Holocene.",
    "task": "The task is to investigate the mechanisms for suppressed El Ni\u00f1o\u2013Southern Oscillation (ENSO) activity during the mid-Holocene by quantitatively analyzing air-sea feedbacks in PMIP2 and PMIP3 model simulations.",
